  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">223756_FY25_WFP_S.Sudan_Fashoda and Panyikang FA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the project is to improve food security for 63,970 shock-affected highly vulnerable households in targeted areas, especially women and youth, through improved livelihoods, resilience and sustainable food systems by 2027.
 
 Specific Objectives include:
 
 Objective 1: To Improve Household food and Nutrition security for 63,970 households in Fashoda and Panyikang Counties.
 
 Objective 2: Improved livelihoods and resilience of 21,000 individuals small-holder farmers and market actors, especially women and youth, for economic empowerment by 2027 &amp;#8211; &amp;#8220;Farming as a business&amp;#8221;
 
 Specific objective 2: To increase school enrolment and retention among 1,900 girls and boys, including children of IDPs, returnees, and refugees in assisted schools at crisis levels through school feeding program.
 
 Objective 3: Improved Natural Resource base for sustainable Livelihoods for 5500HHs in Fashoda
 
 Objective 4: Improved capacities of the disaster-affected population on Accountability and safeguarding</narrative>
  </description>
